  <para style="h">Yọna</para>
  <para style="toc1">Yọna</para>
  <para style="toc2">Yọna</para>
  <para style="toc3">Yọna</para>
  <para style="mt1">Yọna</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="JON 1" />
  <para style="s1">Yọna Afeghe Akpọñ Iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JON 1:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadisịm Yọna ayịn Amitai ate: <verse eid="JON 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JON 1:2" />“Kaa akwa abio Ninife nyʌñ ke kwọrọ ikọ baña anye, sia ibak amọ adinsịm miin.”<verse eid="JON 1:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JON 1:3" />Ado Yọna amaafeghe akpọñ iso Abasi adakka akaa Taasis. Anye amaakaa Yopa, do anye amaakekịt nsʌñikañ keed a-akeyemme adika Taasis. Ke anye amaakekpe akʌk ukpeusʌñ ima, anye amaaboiyo adʌk esịd nsʌñikañ anyʌñ adakka Taasis nọ ato do anye afeghe akpọñ iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="JON 1:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JON 1:4" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadọñ ekamba afịm utom ke akpainyañ, ndin ekamba ayobio amaafịme tutu aba nte nsʌñikañ ayaasakka. <verse eid="JON 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JON 1:5" />Afịd mme awad nsʌñikañ emaekop ndịk enyʌñ etua ekoot abasi ammọ. Ndin ammọ emaesịññe mme mbiomo ke nsʌñikañ etoomo edọñ ke inyañ nọ ato do amaana afeere.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JON 1:5">Ado Yọna amaasọiyọ adʌk idak isọñ nsʌñikañ, akesuuk anaa adaiya se ekoot idab. <verse eid="JON 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JON 1:6" />Etubom nsʌñikañ amaabịne anye akebo, “Afo akpenanam die adaiya utọ idab ami? Dakka da koot abasi mfo! Akemeido anye ayaase ñkpọ ibaña ñnyịn mbaak ñnyịn iditak.”<verse eid="JON 1:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JON 1:7" />Ndin mme awad nsʌñikañ emaebo emọ-emọ ete, “Idi, yak ñnyịn isịn afia idiọọñọ me anie awo inam nọ idiọọkñkpọ ami atịppe inọ ñnyịn.” Ammọ emaesịn afia ndin afia amaatịp Yọna. <verse eid="JON 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JON 1:8" />Ndin ammọ emaebịp anye ete, “Tañ inọ ñnyịn, anie awo inam nọ afịd mfịna ami isịm ñnyịn? Nsoo utọ utom ke afo anam? Afo ato uke? Idịd mfo ado uke? Afo ado awo uke?”<verse eid="JON 1:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JON 1:9" />Anye amaabọọrọ ate, “Ami ndo ayịn Hibru ñnyʌñ ñkpono <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, Abasi anyọñ, a-akenamma akpainyañ ye nsaad isọñ.”<verse eid="JON 1:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JON 1:10" />Ñkpọ ami amaanam ammọ ndịk eti-eti, ndin ammọ emaebịp ete, “Nsoo ke afo anam?” (Ammọ emaediọọñọ ke anye akefeefeghe akpọñ iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, sia anye amaadọdọkkọ ammọ ntoro.)<verse eid="JON 1:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JON 1:11" />Ayobio amaanenekke asọñ itak. Anam ammọ emaebịp anye ete, “Nsoo ke ñnyịn ikpunam fiin nọ ato do inyañ asuuhọ inọ ñnyịn?”<verse eid="JON 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JON 1:12" />Anye amaabọọrọ ate, “Ndufo imben miin itop isịn ke inyañ, ndin inyañ ayaadobo. Mmediọọñọ ke ndudue mmi anam ekamba ayobio ami adisịm ndufo.”<verse eid="JON 1:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JON 1:13" />Utu ke ado, ideen ado emaedomo afịd ukeme ammọ adiwat ntịmme edem ñkewuọ abod. Ado ammọ ikikanna, sia inyañ amaatọtʌm adamma akan naña akedo. <verse eid="JON 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JON 1:14" />Ndin ammọ emaebọñ ekoot <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ete, “Mbọk, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, kuuyak ñnyịn ikpa ke ntak adidat uwem awo ami. Kuudot ñnyịn iyiib awo i-imiidueghe ke iwuod, sia afo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, amenam naña unemme fiin.” <verse eid="JON 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JON 1:15" />Akem ammọ emaeben Yọna etop esio ke ubom, ndin akpainyañ a-akedammake amaadop. <verse eid="JON 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JON 1:16" />Ntom ke ammọ ekebaak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> eti-eti, ndin ammọ emaewa uwa enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> enyʌñ ekaaña akaaña enọ anye.<verse eid="JON 1:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Akam Yọna</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JON 1:17" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanịm ataa ekamba iyak nọ aben Yọna amen, ndin anye amaanyʌñ asịne ke idịb iyak ado uweemeayio ita ye akonayio ita.<verse eid="JON 1:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JON 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="JON 2" />
  <para style="nb">
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">2: </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke mme ikpañwed Hibru ewet Yọọn 2:1 nte Yọọn 1:17, ñko ewet Yọọn 2:1-10 nte Yọọn 2:2-11.</char>
    </note> <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JON 2:1" />Yọna amaasịne ke idịb iyak ado abọñ akam anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi amọ. <verse eid="JON 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JON 2:2" />Anye amaabo ate:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JON 2:2">“Ke ukuud mmi ami mmaakoot <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:2">ndin anye amañyie miin.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JON 2:2">Ñkesịne ke ube ñkpa ñkoot ñyem unwam,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:2">ndin afo amaakop ayịd mmi.<verse eid="JON 2:2" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JON 2:3" />Afo amamben miin atop asịn ke udem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:3">ke ataa esịd akpainyañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:3">ndin ndufịd mmọọñ ayʌt añkanna miin;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JON 2:3">afịd ndufịd ye atọ mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:3">etọ emfʌk miin.<verse eid="JON 2:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JON 2:4" />Ami mmaabo nte, ‘Embịne miin</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:4">esio ke iso mfo;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JON 2:4">kpayeado ñyaamaana nse</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:4">adisana tembịd mfo.’<verse eid="JON 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JON 2:5" />Mme mmọọñ e-eñkannake miin ekʌk ennam miin ndịk,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:5">udem añkanna miin akʌk;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:5">mbid akpainyañ añwaña miin ke iwuod akanna.<verse eid="JON 2:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JON 2:6" />Ami mmaatịkke ñkewuọ adʌñ ikpọabod;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:6">idak isọñ abet usʌñ ansịn ke nsi-nsi.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JON 2:6">Ado afo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mmi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:6">amaasio uwem mmi ke ube afep.<verse eid="JON 2:6" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JON 2:7" />“Ke ini uwem mmi akebaaha nte ayaaboiyo ifep,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:7">ami mmautoiyo fiin, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JON 2:7">ndin akam mmi amaadọọk ubịne fiin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:7">ke adisana tembịd mfo.<verse eid="JON 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JON 2:8" />“Mbon e-eyịreke mme ikpu-ikpu ubobodñkpọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:8">e-ekpa edem ewọt ima a-Abasi anieghe anọ ammọ.<verse eid="JON 2:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JON 2:9" />Ado ami ñyaadat ñkpo itooro ekọọm,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:9">ñwa uwa unọ fiin.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JON 2:9">Se ñnwọñọ ñyaanam.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JON 2:9">Ami ñyaabo, ‘Adinyaaña ato <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="JON 2:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JON 2:10" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanọ iyak ado uyio, anye amaanyʌñ akekọk Yọna asio adot ke nsaad isọñ.<verse eid="JON 2:10" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JON 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="JON 3" />
  <para style="s1">Yọna Akaa Ninife</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JON 3:1" />Ndin ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadisịm Yọna ayọhọ akañ iba ate: <verse eid="JON 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JON 3:2" />“Kaa ekamba abio Ninife nyʌñ kedọkkọ anye etob a-ami unọọhọ fiin.”<verse eid="JON 3:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JON 3:3" />Yọna amaakop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anyʌñ adakka akaa Ninife. Ninife akedo ataa ekamba abio; akedat usen ita adisaña ke esịd amọ. <verse eid="JON 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JON 3:4" />Yọna amaatọọñọ ke adinam isañ usen keed ke abio ado, asaña akwọrọ abo, “Usen aba asʌhọ ndin Ninife ayaaduọ.” <verse eid="JON 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JON 3:5" />Mbon Ninife emaenịm Abasi ke akpanikọ. Emaenịm utreudia, ndin afịd ammọ, tọọñọ ke mme adaaha tutu awuọ andisịb ñkan, emaesịne afọñikpo ke idem.<verse eid="JON 3:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JON 3:6" />Ke ini etob Yọna akekesịmme adidem Ninife, anye amaadakka ada ke ebekpo amọ, asịññe afọñidem ubọọñ amọ ke idem, aben afọñikpo asịne anyʌñ asuuk atie ke ntọñ. <verse eid="JON 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JON 3:7" />Ewʌhọ a-anye akenọọhọ ke Ninife ado ami:</para>
  <para style="pmo" vid="JON 3:7">Etop ami ato adidem ye mme adaaha amọ:</para>
  <para style="pm" vid="JON 3:7">Ikiiyak nọ mme awo me unam, udịmenañ me udịmedọñ ndomokeed esịn ñkpọ ndomokeed ke inua; ikiiyak ammọ edia ñkpọ me enwọñ ñkpọ. <verse eid="JON 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JON 3:8" />Ado yak esịn mme awo ye unam afọñikpo. Yak afịd awo eseeme enọ Abasi usọp-usọp. Yak ammọ ekpọñ idiọọk ido ammọ ye afai uwem. <verse eid="JON 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JON 3:9" />Anie idiọọñọ? Abasi akeme adikpəho akikere anyʌñ akpọñ akpọsọñ iyadesịd amọ akappa ise ñnyịn ye mbọm, mbaak ñnyịn iditak.<verse eid="JON 3:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JON 3:10" />Ke ini Abasi amaakekịt se ammọ ekenam ye naña ammọ ekekpọñ idiọọk ido ammọ, anye amaakpəho akikere, inyʌññọ isobo ammọ naña akeduak.<verse eid="JON 3:10" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JON 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="JON 4" />
  <para style="s1">Iyadesịd Yọna ke Abaña Mbọm <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JON 4:1" />Ado Yọna akedat ami nte ataa idiọọkñkpọ, ndin anye amaayat esịd. <verse eid="JON 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JON 4:2" />Anye amaabọñ akam anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ate, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, idooho se ami ñkebo ado ami, tọọñọ idaha a-ami ñkebaaha ke idʌñ ñnyịn? Se ñkesʌk ñnwana adibọkkọ ado ado ke ini ñkefegheke ñka Taasis. Ami mmaadiọọñọ ke afo ado Abasi mfọn ye mbọm, usọppọ iyadesịd anyʌñ ayọhọ ye ima, Abasi a-akpəhoke akikere abaña adimia awo ufen idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="JON 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JON 4:3" />Ndin idahami, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, dat uwem mmi, sia afọn ami adikpa akan ami adidu uwem.”<verse eid="JON 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JON 4:4" />Ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabọọrọ ate, “Nte anen afo adiyat esịd?”<verse eid="JON 4:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JON 4:5" />Ndin Yọna amaawuọ aketie ke itie keed ke ñkañ usakkautịn abio. Ke ndo, anye amaanam atayad anọ idem amọ, asuuk atie ke mfuud atayad ado abet adikịt se idiitịppe inọ Ninife. <verse eid="JON 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JON 4:6" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi amaanam eto mfañ keed atịppe anyʌñ akọt afʌk Yọna nọ ato do anọ anye mfuud ke iwuod mbaak anye adibọ ufen abọhọ; ndin Yọna amaanekke anem esịd abaña eto ado. <verse eid="JON 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JON 4:7" />Ado ke ubakusen edem usen Abasi amaanọ utʌñ aketa eto ado ndin anye ayeppe. <verse eid="JON 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JON 4:8" />Ke ayio amaakesakka, Abasi amaasio ufiob afịm, ndin ayio amaafọp Yọna iwuod tutu anye akop mmemidem. Anye amaayem adikpa, anyʌñ abo ate, “Akpaafọn ami adikpa akan ami adidu uwem.”<verse eid="JON 4:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JON 4:9" />Ado Abasi amaabo Yọna, “Nte anen afo adiyat esịd mbaña eto ado?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JON 4:9">Anye amaabo, “Anen. Ndin esịd añyat miin tutu ami ñkere ke akpaafọn ami adikpa.”<verse eid="JON 4:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JON 4:10" />Ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo, “Afo amekere ñkpọ abaña eto ami, akpesʌkado umuukunamma utom ke esịd, unyʌññọ unam nọ anye akọt. Aketịppe ada akonayio keed anyʌñ akpa akonayio keed. <verse eid="JON 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JON 4:11" />Nte ikpinaaha ami ndin ñkop mbọm mbaña ekamba abio Ninife, a-mme awo se iwak ikan tọsịn ikie keed mme edịb, i-imiidiọọñọke ukpʌhọde ubọk nnasia ammọ me ufiin, ye uwak unam ñko, e-edʌññọ ke esịd?”<verse eid="JON 4:11" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JON 4" />
</usx>